-- Fuller "About the writer" biographies (2-3 sentences) for the seeded authors.

UPDATE author AS a
SET bio = v.bio
FROM (VALUES
    ('arjun-patel', 'Arjun Patel writes practical guides on focus, productivity and deliberate work. A former software engineer, he turned to writing after years of helping teams ship calmly. His books favour short chapters, honest examples and habits a reader can start the same day.'),
    ('raj-patel', 'Raj Patel is an educator and author who believes learning never stops. He has spent two decades teaching and mentoring, and writes about curiosity, study habits and reinventing yourself at any age. His work is warm, plain-spoken and full of classroom stories.'),
    ('james-wright', 'James Wright writes about goals, habits and quiet confidence. He draws on years of coaching professionals through career changes and turns those conversations into clear, encouraging advice. Readers return to his books for their steady tone and practical exercises.'),
    ('james-adams', 'James Adams is the author of atmospheric mysteries and thrillers set in fog-bound towns and sleeping cities. He plots slowly and lets the setting do much of the haunting. His novels have a loyal readership who like to guess the ending and rarely get it right.'),
    ('jessica-martin', 'Jessica Martin is a romance novelist with a taste for sweeping settings, from hill stations to harbour towns. Her stories pair patient slow-burn love with vivid local detail. She writes each book first as a letter to someone she has never met.'),
    ('laura-mitchell', 'Laura Mitchell writes science fiction inspired by space exploration and the people who make it happen. She grew up reading mission logs as bedtime stories and brings that wonder to her fiction. Her novels balance big ideas with very human crews.'),
    ('daniel-reed', 'Daniel Reed is a champion of simple living and clear thinking. His essays and guides ask readers to own less, decide faster and spend time on what matters. He writes from a small flat with a large bookshelf and one very old desk.'),
    ('clara-nelson', 'Clara Nelson writes chilling stories set in old houses with long memories. She collects local ghost tales and reshapes them into patient, unsettling novels. Her readers are advised to read her books in daylight.'),
    ('emily-parker', 'Emily Parker is a children''s author of animal adventures full of friendship and mischief. A former primary school librarian, she tests every story out loud on a live audience of seven-year-olds. Her books are made for bedtime and for reading twice.'),
    ('priya-nair', 'Priya Nair writes warm stories of love, family and the kitchens where both are made. Her novels follow ordinary households through festivals, quarrels and quiet reconciliations. She lives on the Kerala coast and writes in the early morning before the house wakes.'),
    ('vikram-rao', 'Vikram Rao is a historian and storyteller of trade routes, ports and the people who travelled them. He turns archive records into vivid narrative and loves a good map. His books make long centuries feel like a conversation over tea.'),
    ('ananya-iyer', 'Ananya Iyer writes on history, ideas and everyday philosophy for readers who do not own a philosophy degree. She holds that big questions belong at the dinner table. Her essays are curious, funny and always kind to the reader.'),
    ('rohan-mehta', 'Rohan Mehta is a travel writer and biographer who follows his subjects across borders and decades. He is known for patient research and for finding the small, human detail in a grand story. He writes between journeys, usually on trains.'),
    ('meera-krishnan', 'Meera Krishnan is a food writer who collects recipes and the stories behind them. She has cooked in family kitchens across the country and writes about meals as memory. Her books are as likely to be read in an armchair as at the stove.'),
    ('sanjay-kulkarni', 'Sanjay Kulkarni retells classic epics for new readers, keeping the grandeur and dropping the dust. A lifelong student of Sanskrit and storytelling, he writes in clean, modern prose. His retellings are popular with families who read aloud.'),
    ('kavya-reddy', 'Kavya Reddy is a Telugu novelist and playwright whose work moves between village life and the city stage. Her dialogue is sharp and her characters stubbornly alive. She has seen several of her plays performed in regional theatres.'),
    ('thomas-bennett', 'Thomas Bennett is a science communicator and essayist who explains difficult ideas without talking down. He has spent years writing for general audiences, and his work balances rigour with wit. He is happiest when a reader says they finally understood something.'),
    ('sarah-collins', 'Sarah Collins writes accessible science and personal essays that begin with a small observation and end somewhere surprising. A trained biologist, she brings field notes to the page. Her readers praise her patience and her sense of humour.'),
    ('oliver-grant', 'Oliver Grant is a fantasy author of long, layered series with carefully built worlds. He draws his own maps and keeps a notebook of invented histories. His novels reward readers who like to notice a detail early and see it matter much later.'),
    ('neha-gupta', 'Neha Gupta is a Hindi poet and language teacher who writes for readers of every age. Her poems are short, musical and rooted in everyday life. She believes poetry belongs in classrooms, kitchens and bus stops alike.'),
    ('arvind-swamy', 'Arvind Swamy is a Kannada writer of memoir and mystery. He mixes recollection with suspense, so that even a family story keeps its secrets until the last chapter. He writes in the evenings after a full day as a schoolteacher.'),
    ('lakshmi-narayan', 'Lakshmi Narayan is a Tamil poet, storyteller and teacher. Her work draws on village folktales and the rhythms of classical verse. She has guided generations of students to love their mother tongue.'),
    ('daniel-brooks', 'Daniel Brooks writes young adult fiction and graphic stories about growing up, friendship and finding your voice. He draws on his own awkward teenage years for material. His books are fast, funny and honest about how hard being young can be.'),
    ('isha-verma', 'Isha Verma is a Hindi romance novelist with a gift for tender, everyday love stories. Her characters are neighbours, colleagues and old friends who find each other in small ways. Readers describe her books as a warm shawl on a cool evening.'),
    ('nikhil-sharma', 'Nikhil Sharma writes quiet, claustrophobic science fiction set on lonely stations and long voyages. A former engineer, he is fascinated by what isolation does to people and machines. His stories reward patient readers with a slow, memorable chill.')
) AS v(slug, bio)
WHERE a.slug = v.slug;
